\subsection{Phase-Field Contours, Crack Symmetry, and Localization Profiles}
Figure~\ref{fig:matched_contours_pack} illustrates the full 2D damage field $d(\mathbf{x})$ at representative deformation states.
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Crack Centroid Path $y_c(x)$:} Damage-weighted centroid offset $|y_c - 0.5\,\mathrm{mm}| \le 3.10\,\mu\mathrm{m}$ across all fixed and adaptive meshes, confirming pure Mode-I symmetry within discrete element bounds (Fig.~\ref{fig:path_dev_pack}(a)).
  \item \textbf{Diffusive Band Width:} The moderate damage band ($d \ge 0.50$) spans a transverse full-width of $20.0$--$30.0\,\mu\mathrm{m}$ ($20.0$--$22.9\,\mu\mathrm{m}$ at $x = 0.55\,\mathrm{mm}$), qualified as \textbf{\texttt{MESH-SENSITIVE / RESOLUTION-LIMITED}} (Fig.~\ref{fig:ligament_pack} and \ref{fig:path_dev_pack}(b)).
\end{itemize}

